      "source": "City of Surrey: Corporate Reports",
      "jurisdiction": "Surrey",
      "type": "council",
      "note": "Surrey staff review of the roughly 72,000 properties made SSMUH-eligible inside the Urban Containment Boundary. The city has approved 465 building permits yielding 943 net new units: 71% duplexes, 22% garden suites or coach houses, 7% houseplexes. Engineering estimates $820 to $870 million to upsize 260 km of small diameter water main and 100 km of sanitary sewer over a 40 to 50 year horizon, and warns that without amendments to Subdivision and Development Bylaw 8830 those costs fall on existing ratepayers rather than on developing properties."
    },
